  "early_warning_diagnostic": {
    "definition": "Among VALIDATION sequences with a valid K=5 forecast, group by the sequence's ACTUAL label at t+5 (Benign vs Infilteration). For each group, report the mean/median full-pipeline P(Infiltration) at K=1, K=2, K=3, K=5 for that SAME sequence, restricted at each K to sequences for which that horizon is also individually valid (gap/partition-safe). This tests whether sequences destined to show Infiltration at t+5 already display elevated P(Infiltration) at earlier, shorter lead times, without assuming this must be true and without inventing a numeric 'lead time in seconds' metric. Because Feature 12 verified target windows are genuinely consecutive 1-second windows, horizon K here does correspond to K seconds ahead for the sequences evaluated at that horizon.",
